  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">OCHA Ukraine Humanitarian Fund</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Support to Ukraine Humanitarian Fund (UHF). Under the overall management of OCHA, the UHF supports timely allocation and disbursement of donor resources to the most critical humanitarian needs as defined by Ukraine&#x2019;s annual Humanitarian Response Plan (HRP) and Flash Appeals.

The prioritization in the HRP for Ukraine ensures that the proposed activities are principled, realistic and feasible, considering the severity of people&#x2019;s needs, the characteristics of the population, including age, gender and disabilities in each geographical location. 

The UHF promotes meaningful local partnerships and specifically prioritizes national NGOs including women-led and women rights organizations. All projects are required to incorporate protection principles and promoting meaningful access, safety and dignity in humanitarian aid, including for the prevention, mitigation and response to gender-based violence. Partners who receive support through UHF will use a tailored setup of Gender and Age Marker for the activity-based approach, disability-sensitive programming, the centrality of protection and inclusion of Accountability to the Affected Population (AAP) to ensure high quality programming. Partners are also encouraged to include the needs of children. 

As an example of allocation priorities, the 2023 Second Standard Allocation launched on 30 November 2023 includes the following three priority areas of activities: i) delivery of critical humanitarian assistance to hard-to-reach areas closest to the frontline (30 km) and Russian border (20 km), ii) multi-sectoral and critical single-sector assistance in the raions of high intersectoral needs in the eastern, southern and northern oblasts of Ukraine, and iii) coordinated multi-sectoral assistance to support vulnerable IDPs in prioritized collective sites.</narrative>
  </description>
